# Handshake files the mcp-follow capture uses: the readiness signal the
# `mcp` scene publishes once its server is bound and its TUI has mounted,
# and the gate that then releases the client pane. Created and removed by
# docs/demo/mcp-follow.tape and docs/demo/demo.py, never committed.
.korvid-mcp-demo-go
.korvid-mcp-demo-ready

# The client pane's verdict on its own run, written by docs/demo/mcp_client.py
# and read by the tape once it has stopped recording: VHS records a fixed
# window and cannot tell a complete story from a client that died in the
# middle of one. Recording side effects like the two above, never committed.
.korvid-mcp-demo-client-ok
.korvid-mcp-demo-client-failed
